| Field                                    | Description                                                                          |
| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `min_num_peers`                          | Minimum peers required for block production (default: 3)                             |
| `block_production_tracking_delay`        | Block production tracking delay (default: `{"secs": 0, "nanos": 100000000}` / 100ms) |
| `min_block_production_delay`             | Min block production delay (default: `{"secs": 0, "nanos": 600000000}` / 600ms)      |
| `max_block_production_delay`             | Max block production delay (default: `{"secs": 1, "nanos": 1800000000}` / 1.8s)      |
| `max_block_wait_delay`                   | Max block wait delay (default: `{"secs": 6, "nanos": 0}`)                            |
| `produce_empty_blocks`                   | Produce empty blocks (default: true)                                                 |
| `block_header_fetch_horizon`             | Block header fetch horizon (default: 50)                                             |
| `catchup_step_period`                    | Catchup step period (default: `{"secs": 0, "nanos": 100000000}`)                     |
| `chunk_request_retry_period`             | Chunk request retry period (default: `{"secs": 0, "nanos": 400000000}`)              |
| `header_sync_initial_timeout`            | Header sync initial timeout (default: `{"secs": 10, "nanos": 0}`)                    |
| `header_sync_progress_timeout`           | Header sync progress timeout (default: `{"secs": 2, "nanos": 0}`)                    |
| `header_sync_stall_ban_timeout`          | Header sync stall ban timeout (default: `{"secs": 120, "nanos": 0}`)                 |
| `header_sync_expected_height_per_second` | Expected header sync height per second (default: 10)                                 |
| `sync_check_period`                      | Sync check period (default: `{"secs": 10, "nanos": 0}`)                              |
| `sync_step_period`                       | Sync step period (default: `{"secs": 0, "nanos": 10000000}` / 10ms)                  |
| `doomslug_step_period`                   | Doomslug step period (default: `{"secs": 0, "nanos": 100000000}`)                    |
| `sync_height_threshold`                  | Sync height threshold (default: 1)                                                   |
| `chunk_wait_mult`                        | Chunk wait multiplier (default: `[1, 3]`)                                            |

### Store Section (`store`)

| Field                        | Description                                         |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `path`                       | Path to RocksDB storage (default: null)             |
| `enable_statistics`          | Enable RocksDB statistics (default: false)          |
| `enable_statistics_export`   | Enable statistics export (default: true)            |
| `max_open_files`             | Max open files (default: 10000)                     |
| `col_state_cache_size`       | Column state cache size (default: 3221225472 / 3GB) |
| `col_flat_state_cache_size`  | Flat state cache size (default: 134217728 / 128MB)  |
| `block_size`                 | Block size (default: 16384)                         |
| `enable_receipt_prefetching` | Enable receipt prefetching (default: true)          |

**`store.trie_cache`**

| Field                                  | Description                                                  |
| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `default_max_bytes`                    | Default trie cache max bytes (default: 500000000 / 500MB)    |
| `per_shard_max_bytes`                  | Per-shard cache limits (default: `{"s1.v1": 50000000, ...}`) |
| `shard_cache_deletions_queue_capacity` | Shard cache deletions queue capacity (default: 100000)       |

**`store.view_trie_cache`**

| Field                                  | Description                                                 |
| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| `default_max_bytes`                    | View trie cache max bytes (default: 50000000 / 50MB)        |
| `per_shard_max_bytes`                  | Per-shard view cache limits (default: `{}`)                 |
| `shard_cache_deletions_queue_capacity` | View shard cache deletions queue capacity (default: 100000) |

**`store.sweat_prefetch_receivers`** - `["token.sweat", "vfinal.token.sweat.testnet"]`

**`store.sweat_prefetch_senders`** - `["oracle.sweat", "sweat_the_oracle.testnet"]`

**`store.claim_sweat_prefetch_config`**

```json
[
	{ "receiver": "claim.sweat", "sender": "token.sweat", "method_name": "record_batch_for_hold" },
	{ "receiver": "claim.sweat", "sender": "", "method_name": "claim" }
]
```

**`store.load_mem_tries_for_shards`** - `[]` (empty array)

**`store.load_mem_tries_for_tracked_shards`** - RPC: `false`, Validator: `true`

**`store.state_snapshot_config`**

| Field                 | Description                                                                                                                |
| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `state_snapshot_type` | Snapshot type: "Enabled", "GarbageCollect", "ForcedGarbageCollect", "Rollback", "NoSnapshot", or null (default: "Enabled") |

### State Sync Section (`state_sync`)

**`state_sync.sync`** — sync mechanism. The only valid value is `"Peers"` (default). State parts are fetched directly from peers — no external storage (GCS/S3) is supported anymore.

```json
"state_sync": {
	"sync": "Peers"
}
```

**`state_sync.concurrency`** — parallelism for state sync work.

| Field                  | Description                                                                                              |
| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `apply`                | Concurrent "apply parts" tasks (default: 12). Trie reconstruction; ≈ `cpu_cores - 2` is the safe ceiling. |
| `apply_during_catchup` | Concurrent apply tasks during catchup (default: 1). Leave alone.                                         |
| `peer_downloads`       | Concurrent peer state-part requests (default: 150). Practical ceiling ~80–150 before peers rate-limit.    |
| `per_shard`            | Max parallelism per shard for fairness (default: 24).                                                    |

ℹ️ The schema defaults reflect tuned values for a fast host with 8+ CPU cores, 16 GB+ RAM, and 100+ peer connections. The conservative upstream defaults (apply: 4, peer_downloads: 10, per_shard: 6) are still valid for low-spec hosts. Requires a restart — not hot-reloaded. See the [Performance Tuning](#performance-tuning-state-sync-concurrency--network-peers) subsection below for the full JSON blocks and ceilings, and [boot-nodes](/boot-nodes) for the multi-RPC boot-node discovery script.

**`state_sync.parts_compression_lvl`** — Zstd compression level for state parts (default: 0).

**`state_sync.dump`** — optional config to dump state to external storage. `null` disables dumping. Mostly relevant for archival node operators.

### Performance Tuning (State Sync Concurrency + Network Peers)

The schema defaults now reflect tuned values for a fast host. For lower-spec hosts, dial back:

```json
"state_sync": {
  "sync": "Peers",
  "concurrency": {
    "apply": 12,
    "apply_during_catchup": 1,
    "peer_downloads": 150,
    "per_shard": 24
  },
  "parts_compression_lvl": 0
}
```

Notes:

- `peer_downloads` controls concurrent state-part requests in flight. **Ceiling ~80–150** — past that, peers rate-limit you. Set to 150 successfully on 8-core / 30 GB machine with 100+ peers.
- `apply` is the trie-reconstruction parallelism. **Ceiling ≈ `cpu_cores - 2`** — raising it further causes RocksDB contention. Stays at 12 on 8-core.
- `per_shard` is per-shard fairness cap. 24 works well on 8-core.
- `apply_during_catchup` — leave alone (default 1), this is when the node is also catching up blocks.
- `parts_compression_lvl: 0` skips zstd decompression entirely. Speeds up apply by ~5-15ms per part at the cost of larger download.

Also raise `network.max_num_peers` so a populated `boot_nodes` list (see [boot-nodes](/boot-nodes)) actually translates into more connections:

```json
"network": {
  "max_num_peers": 100,
  "ideal_connections_lo": 60,
  "ideal_connections_hi": 80,
  "minimum_outbound_peers": 16
}
```

Requires a restart (concurrency is not hot-reloaded).

### Epoch Sync Section (`epoch_sync`)

| Field                           | Description                                                                                       |
| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `epoch_sync_horizon_num_epochs` | Epochs behind head beyond which epoch sync is used instead of header sync (default: 2).           |
| `timeout_for_epoch_sync`        | Timeout for epoch-sync requests; node retries indefinitely (default: `{"secs": 60, "nanos": 0}`). |

ℹ️ `state_sync_enabled` (top-level boolean) is the legacy switch — keep it `true` unless you're an archival operator. The actual sync mechanism is chosen by `state_sync.sync`.

### Throttling & Resource Pool (Top-Level)

| Field                                       | Description                                                                                  |
| ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `state_request_throttle_period`            | Throttle window for state requests (default: `{"secs": 30, "nanos": 0}`).                  |
| `state_requests_per_throttle_period`        | Max state requests per throttle period (default: 30). Raise to 60 for high-throughput nodes. |
| `state_request_server_threads`             | Thread pool size for the state-request server (default: 4).                                  |
| `view_client_threads`                      | Thread pool size for view client (default: 4). RPC queries handled here.                    |
| `transaction_request_handler_threads`      | Thread pool size for transaction request handler (default: 4).                                |
| `orphan_state_witness_pool_size`           | Pool size for orphan chunk state witnesses (default: 25).                                   |
| `orphan_state_witness_max_size`            | Max size of an orphan state witness in bytes (default: 40000000 ≈ 40 MB).                   |

### Resharding (Dynamic Shard Reconfiguration)

**`resharding_config`** — parameters for dynamic shard resharding.

| Field              | Description                                                                                  |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `batch_size`       | Soft limit on resharding batch size in bytes (default: 500000 ≈ 500 KB).                    |
| `batch_delay`      | Delay between batches (default: `{"secs": 0, "nanos": 5000000}` / 5 ms).                    |
| `retry_delay`      | Delay between retry attempts on failure (default: `{"secs": 10, "nanos": 0}`).                |
| `initial_delay`    | Initial delay before resharding starts (default: `{"secs": 0, "nanos": 0}`).                  |
| `max_poll_time`    | Max time to poll for resharding state (default: `{"secs": 7200, "nanos": 0}` / 2 hours).    |
| `catch_up_blocks`  | Number of blocks to catch up after resharding (default: 20).                                |

### Transaction Routing

| Field                            | Description                                                                                |
| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `tx_routing_height_horizon`      | If node is not chunk producer within this many blocks, route to upcoming producers (default: 4). |
| `disable_tx_routing`             | If true, don't forward transactions to next chunk producers (default: false).               |
| `produce_chunk_add_transactions_time_limit` | Max time for adding transactions to a chunk (Duration).                      |

### Contract Cache & State Witness

| Field                            | Description                                                                                            |
| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `contract_cache_max_size`        | Max size of the compiled-contract cache (default: 128000000000 ≈ 128 GB).                              |
| `contract_cache_path`            | Path to store contract cache. `null` means default location.                                            |
| `save_latest_witnesses`          | Save observed `ChunkStateWitness` to `DBCol::LatestChunkStateWitnesses` (default: false).            |
| `save_invalid_witnesses`         | Save invalid witnesses to `DBCol::InvalidChunkStateWitnesses` (default: false). Off in production. |

### Key Differences: RPC vs Validator

| Field                               | RPC Default | Validator Default |
| ----------------------------------- | ----------- | ----------------- |
| `tracked_shards_config`             | "AllShards" | "NoShards"        |
| `load_mem_tries_for_tracked_shards` | false       | true              |

